{{!--
  The window's top band: brand, a progress meter, and Cancel. It spans the full width above the
  dossier and the work surface.

  This replaced a horizontal stepper that listed all eleven steps as numbered pills. Two things
  were wrong with that. The stepper was the only progress cue on screen, and the stage head that
  carried the "Step 3 of 9" counter was suppressed on exactly the pick steps that make up most of
  the flow — so on most screens there was no counter at all, only a small underscore under one pill
  in a horizontally-scrolling row. And below 1100px the pill labels were dropped entirely, leaving
  bare numerals: number-only navigation, which is the discoverability anti-pattern that rule exists
  to prevent.

  Both problems come from trying to fit a list of steps across the top of a window. The list moved
  to the dossier, where it is vertical and its labels always fit at any width. What is left here is
  the one thing a bar across the top is actually good at: a single measure of how far through the
  player is, always visible, on every step.

  `progress` comes from the shell's #progressContext(). The bar and the "Step 3 of 10" beside it
  are one reading, not two: `done`/`total`/`percent` are the position counts, so the fill is simply
  the graphic of that label and the two can never contradict each other. (They did — the fill used
  to measure completed required steps, which drew a full bar beside "Step 9 of 10" the moment
  everything but Review was done, and a full bar reads as "finished" on a screen where the player
  has not pressed Create.)

  `outstanding` — how many required steps still need input — is the separate question, and gets its
  own readout: teal, because it is the standing answer to "what is left", and absent at zero rather
  than reading "0 outstanding", which would be a thing to parse instead of a thing to notice.
--}}
<header class="creator-topbar">
  <div class="creator-topbar-brand">
    <span>{{localize "sogrom-dnd5e-character-creator.window.brand"}}</span>
    {{#if version}}<span class="creator-topbar-version">v{{version}}</span>{{/if}}
  </div>

  <div class="creator-topbar-progress">
    <div class="creator-progress-track" role="progressbar"
         aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="{{progress.total}}" aria-valuenow="{{progress.done}}"
         aria-label="{{localize 'sogrom-dnd5e-character-creator.dossier.progressAria'}}">
      <div class="creator-progress-fill" style="width: {{progress.percent}}%"></div>
    </div>
    <span class="creator-progress-read">
      <span class="creator-progress-pos">{{progress.position}}</span>
      {{#if progress.outstanding}}
      <span class="creator-progress-todo">{{progress.outstandingLabel}}</span>
      {{/if}}
    </span>
  </div>

  <div class="creator-topbar-foot">
    <button type="button" class="creator-btn creator-btn-ghost" data-action="cancel">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark"></i> {{cancelLabel}}
    </button>
  </div>
</header>
